<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/PA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Text listed in ABBR Group. Abbreviations listed in ABBR group. Rule 16 refers.\nThe list of standard abbreviations and descriptions are presented on the AGS website and shall not be redefined.\nOther abbreviations may be defined as required within a project, but shall not match/impersonate existing standard abbreviations\ne.g. \"CP\" for 'Cable percussion' in LOCA_TYPE shall not be given a non-standard abbreviation defined as \"CH\" for 'Cable hole'; likewise \"SCP\" (Static cone penetrometer) shall not be replaced by a non-standard abbreviation of \"CPT\" (Cone penetration test).\nMultiple abbreviations can be used in a data VARIABLE. Where this occurs, abbreviations are joined using the concatenation character defined in TRAN_RCON (a \"+\" character by default)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types/PA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/data-types> .
