<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary/CPTM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The CPTM group is to be used to define the corelation methods/references for data in the CPTP group.\nIt is envisaged additional custom headings shall be specified in CPTM & CPTP if more methods are to be transmitted. For example, a second heading for Constrained modulus, M 2 would be CPTM_M2 and CPTP_M2.\nIf the method or constant changes with depth, the changes would be documented by a new row in CPTM."@en .
