<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary/FRAC> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "FRAC is used to include fracture spacing derived from rock core, scanline surveys of rock exposures or similar.\nIt is not typical to define fracture set spacing s as both min/avg/max fracture spacing and Fracture Index. The requirement for one or other should be specified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary/FRAC> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Group rules: FRAC_IMAX, FRAC_IAVE, FRAC_IMIN and FRAC_FI shall generally be numeric data. A text form shall only be used by addition of a prefixing operator to denote greater than or less than conditions i.e. >200 or for 'Not intact' (NI)."@en .
