<https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary/RPLT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A list has been defined for RPLT_PLTF to include the test abbreviations derived from the ISRM Suggested Method (ISRM, 2007). Typically a test will include combined abbreviations to represent the sample type/orientation and the direction of the test with respect to bedding. For example a piece of core tested across the diameter and along the bedding direction will be coded as A+L. Reference: ISRM: 2007 : The Complete ISRM Suggested Methods for Rock Characterisation , Testing and Monitoring : 1974-2006."@en .
